+# Hi02 Normalmap run comparison (2026-10-20)
+
+Two separate Release-client starts used the same Hi02 save and render options;
+only `--render-normal-maps=on|off` differed. Both logs reached `UI: Interface
+loaded` and `Game: Entering system Hi02`. The player was invulnerable. The
+renderer was Mesa OpenGL 4.5 on llvmpipe, with a 640x480 client window.
+
+## Images
+
+![Hi02 run with normal maps enabled and disabled](comparison.png)
+
+- [Normal maps on](normalmaps-on.png)
+- [Normal maps off](normalmaps-off.png)
+
+These are captures from separate runs, not the same paused frame. The planet,
+nebula and particle positions changed between captures, so their pixel
+variation cannot be attributed to normal mapping. The player save uses the
+`ge_fighter` archetype, which resolves to the Starflier model and
+`cv_ships.mat`; this run did not establish whether its material uses a mapped
+surface texture. The images therefore document the option and the scene, not a
+positive visual acceptance of Normal Maps.
+
+Both runs used `qa-profile-save.fl`, `--invulnerable=on`, surface PBR maps on,
+PBR environment and diffuse IBL off, HDR on, and Bloom, SSAO, shadows, soft
+particles and particle effects off. Dynamic lighting was on. Logs remain in the
+local NAP staging folders `pbr-samescene-20261020/state-xvfb/` and
+`pbr-samescene-20261020/state-normal-off/`.
+
+The active snapshot is included as [active.json](active.json). Its 14 archives
+matched the declared sizes and SHA-256 hashes; the release and NAP-stage
+snapshots were identical. Those archives were staged from `Data/NAP/`.
